# eb73be3 -- the cancellation chain made applicable, reachable and declared.
# ELEVEN governance commits arrive with this pin, and it is the e802469 hazard
# in a new direction: the hazard there was a file DECLARED but absent from
# disk. Here the declaration NAMES A VOCABULARY that only exists from this
# commit. deploy_state now points the three cancellation files at
# _APPLIED_LOCAL_CANCELLATION_AUTHORITY, _..._ENFORCEMENT and _..._REVERSAL,
# and DISPOSITIONS admits those three names only at eb73be3 -- so a public
# commit pinned earlier fails test_sql_disposition_governance with
# "disposition(s) outside the declared vocabulary", not with anything about
# the SQL. The three _PENDING_CANCELLATION_* names are RETAINED in that set,
# because it spans every state deploy_state is promotable through.
#
# THE BASELINE CHANGED AND CI BUILDS FROM IT. 00_base_schema now installs
# pgcrypto and uuid-ossp into `extensions` rather than public, matching the
# layout measured on both deployed databases. That is not cosmetic: it had been
# installing pgcrypto into public, so every disposable database resolved an
# unqualified digest() that no real database resolves, and the cancellation
# artifacts passed the whole suite and then failed the first statement of a
# real apply. All eleven functions in the three artifacts now pin
# `pg_catalog, public, extensions, pg_temp`; a missing schema in search_path is
# ignored rather than an error, so a pinned function works under either layout.
# test_pgcrypto_search_path keys on unqualified AND unpinned, because
# unqualified with a pin is the working production pattern.
#
# NOT PROMOTED INTO REQUIRED_MIGRATIONS, and the declarations say why in terms:
# all three are APPLIED TO LOCAL railwayl2 with attestation ids 188, 170 and
# 171, and NOT YET ON RAILWAY -- measured object by object, read-only, with
# zero apply_sql attestations there. Promotion belongs in the change that
# records the Railway application.
#
# ONE SECURITY CHANGE TRAVELS WITH IT. fn_cancellation_proposition is now
# SECURITY DEFINER, because a search_path pin is INERT for a role without USAGE
# on the pinned schema: crm_app holds EXECUTE on extensions.digest and not
# USAGE on extensions, and PostgreSQL skips a schema the role cannot enter, so
# the call failed as "function digest does not exist" and read as a missing
# pin. Granting crm_app USAGE was the alternative and was rejected on
# measurement -- 55 of the 56 functions in that schema already carry EXECUTE
# for it, so schema USAGE is the only gate holding them shut. The keyword lives
# in the artifact and not in a later ALTER because CREATE OR REPLACE resets
# prosecdef to the default; the ACL is not reset that way, which is why the
# grants could have lived elsewhere and the security mode could not.
#
# THE PIN MOVES IN A FOLLOW-UP COMMIT AGAIN, for the reason recorded at ded0dbb:
# test_the_pin_names_a_commit_that_actually_exists requires the target to be
# reachable, so eb73be3 could not be named until it was pushed. Its remote
# resolution was verified with ls-remote before this line was written, rather
# than inferred from a successful push.
